# Line endings.
#
# Everything here that is deployed to the Linux server must be LF in the
# WORKING TREE, not only in the repository. `* text=auto` on its own
# normalises to LF on commit and then hands Windows CRLF back on checkout,
# which is a quiet trap in this repo:
#
#   * the patchers read and write with newline="", so a CRLF working copy
#     produces a CRLF app.py, which is then not byte-identical to the file on
#     the server -- the property every deploy here is verified against;
#   * tools/CHECK_FOLDER_PARITY.py compares the working folder against the app
#     folders, and both would be CRLF, so it would pass while the server
#     disagreed with both.
#
# Measured 2026-09-14, before this file was corrected: a fresh clone produced
# gutlog/app.py at 265,085 bytes with 4,999 CR bytes, against 260,086 on the
# server. The committed blobs were right; the checkout was not.
#
# So declare LF explicitly for everything that ships, and let the Windows
# launchers keep CRLF -- cmd.exe is not reliable with LF-only labels and goto.

* text=auto

# --- deployed to the server: LF in the working tree too --------------------
*.py          text eol=lf
*.json        text eol=lf
*.js          text eol=lf
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.service     text eol=lf
*.logrotate   text eol=lf
*.txt         text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf
*.example     text eol=lf

# --- Windows-only launchers: keep CRLF -------------------------------------
*.bat         text eol=crlf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore    text eol=lf

# --- binary: never converted, never diffed as text -------------------------
*.png         binary
*.zip         binary
*.pdf         binary
